  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A simulator and parameter-calibration prototype for microalgal photobioreactors. It fits Monod-type nitrogen- and light-limited growth models to batch-culture biomass and nitrate data, checks whether each parameter can be estimated using profile-likelihood intervals, and exports a report that records where everything came from. It also simulates model variants and operating conditions. Other workspaces cover model comparison and next-experiment planning, OD/cell-count calibration, joint calibration across runs, and light × nitrogen scenario planning. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
  "source": {
